<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50598" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰόνιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰώ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>called after Io</i>, epith. of
			the sea between Epirus and Italy, at the mouth of the Adriatic sea,
			across which Io swam, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντιος μυχὸς . . Ἰόνιος κεκλήσεται,
					τῆς σῆς πορείας μνῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					840
				</span></i>
			; another expl. in <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Hist.
				125
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰ. κόλπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.127
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα, πόρος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				3.68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				4.53
			</span></i>; also simply 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Ἰόνιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.30
				</span></i>
			; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰόνιον πέλαγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.251
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
